# Call-site ledger of pyrate-limiter at 968301de411f722235c6db152a55fa4ea77fd3c7.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in pyrate-limiter.md.
#
# Dispatch sets used below (pyrate-limiter.md, "Dispatch sets"):
#   buckets (7 concrete, all public): InMemoryBucket, MultiprocessBucket
#     (inherits InMemoryBucket's count, flush, peek), StateBucket, RedisBucket,
#     PostgresBucket, SQLiteBucket, BucketAsyncWrapper. AbstractBucket is
#     abstract by abc; client subclasses are client code.
#   log algorithms: SlidingWindowLog, FixedWindow (FixedWindow inherits
#     LogAlgorithm.blocking_offset; both inherit Algorithm.max_weight).
#   state algorithms: GCRA, TokenBucket (TokenBucket adds nothing).
#   state stores: InMemoryStateStore, MultiprocessStateStore, RedisStateStore
#     (none overrides StateStore.close).
#   clocks: MonotonicClock, WallClock, MonotonicAsyncClock, PostgresClock,
#     SQLiteClock (AbstractClock is abstract).
#   bucket factories: SingleBucketFactory; BucketFactory is abstract and the
#     client's factories are client code.
# redis, psycopg, psycopg_pool and aiohttp are not installed in the test
# environment: their calls are named as missing modules (judgement 7).
default reject pyrate_limiter.abstracts.rate.Duration.__eq__: no Duration member is compared, searched with `in`, hashed into a dict or set, or used as a key at this site; Rate.__init__ turns a Duration interval into an int at once (int(interval), rate.py:95), so the package compares, subscripts and looks up only ints, floats, strs, bytes, bools, None, tuples, lists, dicts, sqlite and database rows, and typing constructs in annotations
default reject pyrate_limiter.abstracts.rate.Rate.__repr__: no Rate, and no container of Rates, is formatted, interpolated, logged or converted to str at this site; the values are ints, floats, strs, bytes, types, rows and SQL templates (utils.py:42:46 formats a list of Rates and accepts the candidate explicitly)
default reject pyrate_limiter.abstracts.rate.Rate.__str__: no Rate is formatted, interpolated or converted to str by itself at this site; the only Rates that the package formats are elements of a list, whose str() calls repr() on each element (Rate.__repr__)
default reject pyrate_limiter.abstracts.rate.RateItem.__str__: no RateItem is formatted, interpolated or converted to str at this site; the values are ints, floats, strs, bytes, types, rows and SQL templates, and a RateItem's name is the client's str key
default reject pyrate_limiter.abstracts.bucket.AbstractBucket.__enter__, pyrate_limiter.abstracts.bucket.AbstractBucket.__exit__, pyrate_limiter.limiter.Limiter.__enter__, pyrate_limiter.limiter.Limiter.__exit__: no `with` statement of the package manages a bucket or a Limiter; the managers are threading and multiprocessing locks, a FileLock or a client lock, contextlib.nullcontext, the context managers of combined_lock and PostgresBucket._get_conn, and psycopg_pool connections and cursors

